1
00:00:09,642 --> 00:00:12,019
The sacred site where the Dofus were placed

2
00:00:13,020 --> 00:00:16,523
is fiercely protected by legendary beings,

3
00:00:16,690 --> 00:00:20,527
the fearsome Bellaphones, whose magic defies the ages.

4
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:12,890
EPISODE 4 CARAMELIZED KEBABS

5
00:02:38,290 --> 00:02:39,708
Eggs...

6
00:02:40,584 --> 00:02:42,044
and tea.

7
00:02:42,628 --> 00:02:45,172
They took time to rest.

8
00:02:50,010 --> 00:02:51,637
What is it, Sipho?

9
00:02:51,804 --> 00:02:53,847
Have you picked up their trail?

10
00:02:54,014 --> 00:02:56,934
The fugitives definitely spent the night here, Prince.

11
00:02:57,810 --> 00:02:59,228
They found support.

12
00:02:59,395 --> 00:03:00,938
Their group has grown.

13
00:03:01,105 --> 00:03:03,607
This house is full of odors of all kinds.

14
00:03:04,566 --> 00:03:07,361
The smell of sweat is getting in the way.

15
00:03:08,404 --> 00:03:12,449
Still, I'm sure that there were at least three people here

16
00:03:12,616 --> 00:03:14,326
in addition to your cousin.

17
00:03:14,785 --> 00:03:16,328
And... a cat.

18
00:03:18,205 --> 00:03:20,958
Clearly, my mother has enemies everywhere.

19
00:03:25,921 --> 00:03:27,589
The embers are still hot.

20
00:03:27,756 --> 00:03:29,717
Let's not dawdle. They must be near.

21
00:03:30,801 --> 00:03:32,177
Indeed,

22
00:03:32,344 --> 00:03:34,680
we've clearly just missed them.

23
00:03:34,847 --> 00:03:37,516
Everything indicates that they left in a hurry.

24
00:03:47,901 --> 00:03:50,571
I can smell my father's poison.

25
00:03:50,737 --> 00:03:53,741
It's the young man who's affected. He's gravely ill.

26
00:03:54,366 --> 00:03:57,619
Who knows, he might have even passed away already.

27
00:03:58,454 --> 00:04:01,999
If not yet, soon. There's no way he can survive, Prince.

28
00:04:02,541 --> 00:04:05,335
Good. Lead me to him immediately, Sipho,

29
00:04:05,502 --> 00:04:07,880
so I can prove his death to my mother.

30
00:04:17,514 --> 00:04:18,724
Mama...

31
00:04:18,891 --> 00:04:21,018
can you take the gratin out?

32
00:04:22,227 --> 00:04:25,481
I still have to cut the carrots and peel the onions...

33
00:04:27,941 --> 00:04:29,401
They make my eyes water.

34
00:04:30,194 --> 00:04:32,571
Say, since it's nice out,

35
00:04:33,071 --> 00:04:36,575
do you want me to make those kebabs you like so much?

36
00:04:47,127 --> 00:04:50,172
- Dad? - I'm fine. Don't worry about me.

37
00:04:50,923 --> 00:04:54,635
But you're coughing more and more. It's really hard not to worry.

38
00:05:02,184 --> 00:05:05,395
We'll start by making the marinade.

39
00:05:09,024 --> 00:05:11,068
We mix a spoonful of mustard

40
00:05:11,235 --> 00:05:13,111
with a clove of minced garlic.

41
00:05:14,363 --> 00:05:16,615
Then, we add the olive oil,

42
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:21,787
honey for a hint of sweetness and a little lemon for acidity.

43
00:05:21,954 --> 00:05:24,039
Are you using Bechamel's honey?

44
00:05:24,206 --> 00:05:25,332
Of course.

45
00:05:26,166 --> 00:05:28,585
Bechamel's honey is the best.

46
00:05:37,970 --> 00:05:39,972
And we can't forget the herbs.

47
00:05:40,138 --> 00:05:41,849
Rosemary, for example.

48
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:58,865
The secret is in the amount of each ingredient.

49
00:05:59,032 --> 00:06:00,158
What I really love...

50
00:06:00,325 --> 00:06:01,535
...Is cooking.

51
00:06:02,077 --> 00:06:05,122
You're fighting in your own way, Welsh. Hang in there.

52
00:06:06,665 --> 00:06:08,584
I've got a bad feeling, lil' pal.

53
00:06:08,750 --> 00:06:12,004
The poor kid seems to be doing poorly. He's delirious.

54
00:06:12,713 --> 00:06:15,299
It's my fault. How could I be so stupid?

55
00:06:15,465 --> 00:06:17,885
Asalar poisoned him right in front of me

56
00:06:18,051 --> 00:06:19,761
and I didn't even realize it.

57
00:06:20,137 --> 00:06:22,222
Nobody caught it, Jojo.

58
00:06:22,389 --> 00:06:25,017
Stop beating yourself up over what happened.

59
00:06:25,183 --> 00:06:27,895
Instead, focus on what you can do for him now.

60
00:06:28,228 --> 00:06:30,856
It's happening too fast, Khan. We aren't ready.

61
00:06:31,023 --> 00:06:32,524
I don't know what to do.

62
00:06:32,691 --> 00:06:34,484
One thing at a time!

63
00:06:35,611 --> 00:06:37,946
First, we take the kid to get healed.

64
00:06:38,697 --> 00:06:41,992
I'll be surprised if your healer can cure dragon poison.

65
00:06:42,159 --> 00:06:44,536
- This is Asalar, after all. - Master Joris,

66
00:06:44,995 --> 00:06:48,832
if you hadn't stepped in, that monster would have killed Welsh.

67
00:06:48,999 --> 00:06:53,420
You've already saved him once. I understand you have doubts,

68
00:06:53,587 --> 00:06:56,423
but please, please, don't give up!

69
00:06:58,508 --> 00:07:00,177
I'm sorry, kiddo.

70
00:07:00,510 --> 00:07:03,221
The little girl's right. Stop with the drama.

71
00:07:03,388 --> 00:07:06,183
Keep your hopes up, Uncle. We can save Welsh.

72
00:07:06,350 --> 00:07:09,144
The guy we're going to has cared for dad for years.

73
00:07:09,311 --> 00:07:11,021
That's true. We can trust him.

74
00:07:11,188 --> 00:07:15,067
He's a very good healer and we're barely three hours away.

75
00:07:17,569 --> 00:07:21,073
Right. In any case, I don't have any better suggestions.

76
00:07:21,239 --> 00:07:24,826
Khan, we'll pick up the pace. Do you want me to take a turn?

77
00:07:28,955 --> 00:07:31,750
No, I'm good for now, lil' pal.

78
00:07:31,917 --> 00:07:32,959
Okay, let's go!

79
00:07:35,587 --> 00:07:38,548
What gives you the right to call me a "little girl"?

80
00:07:38,715 --> 00:07:41,969
I'll have you know we're the same age! So knock it off!

81
00:07:42,886 --> 00:07:45,639
See that, sisters? The little girl is touchy.

82
00:07:46,306 --> 00:07:48,642
Leave poor Bechamel alone, Tess.

83
00:07:48,809 --> 00:07:51,979
She's worried about her cook. Tease her another time.

84
00:07:52,312 --> 00:07:54,314
Oh, yes. She's so cute.

85
00:07:54,481 --> 00:07:57,609
And she's obviously got a huge crush on the young king!

86
00:07:58,902 --> 00:08:00,862
Isn't love grand!

87
00:08:05,117 --> 00:08:06,618
Well? What happened?

88
00:08:06,785 --> 00:08:09,246
For an athlete, your balance is a little off.

89
00:08:09,413 --> 00:08:10,455
Too bad, so sad.

90
00:08:10,622 --> 00:08:13,667
Your team must really suck on the gobbowl field.

91
00:08:17,796 --> 00:08:21,633
This one's got spunk and a quick wit. Don't you agree, girls?

92
00:08:25,303 --> 00:08:26,513
Absolutely!

93
00:08:26,972 --> 00:08:29,891
I've got to admit, she's really growing on me!

94
00:08:54,750 --> 00:08:56,293
We've arrived, friends!

95
00:08:58,045 --> 00:09:02,049
If anyone can heal our young king, it'll be old Cristone.

96
00:09:02,424 --> 00:09:04,051
Great! We're almost there!

97
00:09:04,217 --> 00:09:07,804
Hear that, Welsh? Hang in there a bit longer, he'll cure you!

98
00:09:12,517 --> 00:09:14,478
We made it sooner than I thought.

99
00:09:14,644 --> 00:09:17,397
Come on, luck might finally be on our side.

100
00:09:17,564 --> 00:09:19,816
Luck? I don't think so, Master Joris.

101
00:09:22,778 --> 00:09:25,363
I've heard so much about you.

102
00:09:25,530 --> 00:09:28,492
My mother searched for you in vain for many years

103
00:09:28,658 --> 00:09:31,703
before giving up and forgetting about your existence.

104
00:09:32,037 --> 00:09:32,954
Shedar...

105
00:09:33,330 --> 00:09:36,083
That's "Prince" Shedar! Watch your mouth!

106
00:09:36,583 --> 00:09:38,210
How is your young companion?

107
00:09:38,919 --> 00:09:42,089
The one who dares rise up against my mother. Is he dead?

108
00:09:44,007 --> 00:09:46,510
He's not rising up against anyone!

109
00:09:46,676 --> 00:09:48,220
All he wants to do is cook!

110
00:09:49,012 --> 00:09:51,181
That's not what a dragon said.

111
00:09:51,348 --> 00:09:56,353
He told me a Brassican boy with azure eyes would overthrow my mother by any means.

112
00:09:56,895 --> 00:09:59,856
What? A dragon? Which dragon are you talking about?

113
00:10:00,232 --> 00:10:02,901
Well, Master Joris, if you really want to know,

114
00:10:03,068 --> 00:10:05,362
it was Dardondakal, the white dragon.

115
00:10:06,905 --> 00:10:08,365
No, that's not possible.

116
00:10:08,532 --> 00:10:11,117
Dardondakal was King Kannell's faithful ally.

117
00:10:11,284 --> 00:10:13,703
Why would he want to betray Kannell's son?

118
00:10:13,870 --> 00:10:15,705
You know dragons well enough

119
00:10:15,872 --> 00:10:19,292
to know that they answer to no logic but their own.

120
00:10:20,585 --> 00:10:23,880
Hear me out, Shedar! There are things you don't know!

121
00:10:24,297 --> 00:10:26,466
- Welsh is none other than... - Welsh?

122
00:10:26,633 --> 00:10:29,636
So that's the name of he who dares defy my mother.

123
00:10:31,179 --> 00:10:34,349
Or rather, the puppet you're hiding behind?

124
00:10:34,516 --> 00:10:36,476
But you aren't fooling anyone, Joris.

125
00:10:36,643 --> 00:10:40,897
I know that you're the one plotting, pulling strings from the shadows.

126
00:10:41,231 --> 00:10:44,151
Welsh is the only son of Kannell and Annette.

127
00:10:44,317 --> 00:10:46,278
He's the legitimate heir of Bonta.

128
00:10:46,653 --> 00:10:48,864
The legitimate heir, you say?

129
00:10:49,239 --> 00:10:52,993
If I've understood, you simply hid the child for 16 years.

130
00:10:53,159 --> 00:10:56,329
Were you just biding time before stealing the throne?

131
00:10:56,496 --> 00:10:57,956
But how could he reign?

132
00:10:58,123 --> 00:11:00,834
How could a cook know better than the queen

133
00:11:01,001 --> 00:11:02,794
what is good for the kingdom?

134
00:11:04,212 --> 00:11:06,089
Have you lost your mind

135
00:11:06,256 --> 00:11:09,384
or has your desire for revenge blinded you?

136
00:11:09,551 --> 00:11:11,261
Your mother is a tyrant, kid.

137
00:11:11,428 --> 00:11:14,681
Bonta and Amakna have become the saddest nations.

138
00:11:15,181 --> 00:11:18,185
How dare you insult your queen? She made Bonta...

139
00:11:18,643 --> 00:11:21,771
I'll make a diversion. Get ready to scamper, girls.

140
00:11:22,022 --> 00:11:23,481
Khan Karkass!

141
00:11:24,316 --> 00:11:26,985
Don't be surprised that I recognized you.

142
00:11:27,152 --> 00:11:31,072
Who hasn't seen your statue at the Bonta gobbowl stadium?

143
00:11:32,365 --> 00:11:34,075
You, too, are a legend.

144
00:11:36,661 --> 00:11:40,582
What could have possibly brought you out of retirement?

145
00:11:41,333 --> 00:11:43,084
Who does he think he is?

146
00:11:43,251 --> 00:11:45,462
He's a know-it-all, spoiled prince.

147
00:11:45,879 --> 00:11:47,923
Adventure called. What do you expect?

148
00:11:48,089 --> 00:11:51,217
Age doesn't change you, and I never could resist.

149
00:11:51,384 --> 00:11:53,386
Even risking your daughters' lives?

150
00:11:53,553 --> 00:11:54,471
No,

151
00:11:54,638 --> 00:11:55,722
I don't believe that.

152
00:11:55,889 --> 00:11:58,391
You must have a good reason to get involved.

153
00:11:58,558 --> 00:12:00,602
But that doesn't matter now.

154
00:12:01,853 --> 00:12:04,481
He's got a Dofus. The Emerald Dofus...

155
00:12:17,327 --> 00:12:20,622
Let my daughters leave, they aren't part of this!

156
00:12:21,039 --> 00:12:24,334
You're the one who dragged them into this coup d'état.

157
00:12:24,501 --> 00:12:26,503
You should have thought of them!

158
00:12:26,670 --> 00:12:30,882
By traitorously supporting Kannell's son, you condemned them.

159
00:12:31,049 --> 00:12:33,134
You shouldn't have betrayed the queen

160
00:12:33,301 --> 00:12:36,513
who's sacrificed herself for the good of her subjects!

161
00:12:40,141 --> 00:12:42,269
You were both great heroes

162
00:12:42,435 --> 00:12:44,020
and Bonta owes you a lot.

163
00:12:44,521 --> 00:12:46,022
But now that I see you,

164
00:12:46,189 --> 00:12:49,526
you seem to be pitiful remnants of bygone times.

165
00:12:49,901 --> 00:12:51,027
Master Joris,

166
00:12:51,194 --> 00:12:53,530
please, tell me you have a plan.

167
00:12:54,239 --> 00:12:55,323
Dad!

168
00:12:55,865 --> 00:12:58,535
Stop, Shedar! Give me a chance to explain!

169
00:12:58,910 --> 00:13:01,413
No, traitor, there's nothing left to explain!

170
00:13:08,086 --> 00:13:11,548
My sweet girls, you are so much like your mother.

171
00:13:24,811 --> 00:13:26,354
They're done for, Prince.

172
00:13:26,521 --> 00:13:28,773
No one could survive that fall.

173
00:13:29,315 --> 00:13:30,567
I know, Sipho.

174
00:13:30,734 --> 00:13:33,820
Your mother will be proud of you. You can rejoice.

175
00:13:41,077 --> 00:13:43,496
That's just what I was thinking.

176
00:13:44,497 --> 00:13:46,958
My mother should be satisfied.

177
00:13:49,794 --> 00:13:51,296
Yet, strangely,

178
00:13:51,463 --> 00:13:53,465
nothing about this makes me happy.

179
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:05,602
Dad!

180
00:14:10,482 --> 00:14:13,943
Mama, the meat is really good. Should we make kebabs?

181
00:14:17,197 --> 00:14:18,406
Hey, Khan!

182
00:14:19,032 --> 00:14:22,619
I hope you've kept some of your legendary accuracy.

183
00:14:23,953 --> 00:14:28,208
I won't lie, it's not what it used to be. But the next generation is ready!

184
00:14:28,375 --> 00:14:31,127
I have three talented girls. Right, girls?

185
00:14:34,214 --> 00:14:35,632
Girls, it's the final!

186
00:14:42,764 --> 00:14:44,057
The final?

187
00:14:45,058 --> 00:14:48,520
Yes, girls! And you'll win this match, I'm sure of it!

188
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:50,647
Ready! Take this ball!

189
00:14:51,439 --> 00:14:54,150
Bechamel! We're going to create a portal!

190
00:14:54,317 --> 00:14:56,444
Like the one that took us to Khan's.

191
00:14:56,611 --> 00:14:59,280
It'll appear below us. Keep Welsh with you.

192
00:15:00,073 --> 00:15:01,491
Don't let go of him!

193
00:15:01,658 --> 00:15:03,326
Okay! I've got him!

194
00:15:03,701 --> 00:15:05,036
Go for it, Master Joris!

195
00:15:05,787 --> 00:15:07,038
Is everybody ready?

196
00:15:10,708 --> 00:15:12,544
I'm counting on you!

197
00:15:14,212 --> 00:15:16,047
Our lives are in your hands!

198
00:15:17,173 --> 00:15:18,049
Three,

199
00:15:18,216 --> 00:15:19,050
two,

200
00:15:19,676 --> 00:15:20,718
one...

201
00:15:24,222 --> 00:15:25,682
- Khan! - Yeah, lil' pal?

202
00:15:25,849 --> 00:15:28,017
You were supposed to throw on zero!

203
00:15:28,184 --> 00:15:29,185
On zero?

204
00:15:29,644 --> 00:15:31,312
How could I know that?

205
00:15:34,816 --> 00:15:37,360
Don't give me that. Everybody makes mistakes.

206
00:15:37,527 --> 00:15:39,821
Come on, girls. The throw is at zero!

207
00:15:39,988 --> 00:15:42,073
Don't worry. We've got it, Uncle!

208
00:15:42,574 --> 00:15:44,576
Three, two,

209
00:15:44,742 --> 00:15:45,577
one,

210
00:15:46,119 --> 00:15:47,245
zero!

211
00:15:50,748 --> 00:15:52,250
No! Missed...

212
00:16:20,862 --> 00:16:22,155
Careful, Khan!

213
00:16:24,782 --> 00:16:26,659
Ah, that's gonna hurt.

214
00:16:33,458 --> 00:16:34,542
Kara!

215
00:16:42,592 --> 00:16:44,928
Don't worry, Dad, I've got this.

216
00:16:49,807 --> 00:16:50,850
That's good, girls.

217
00:16:51,017 --> 00:16:55,188
Now get out of the way, fast, before you take a blow to the head!

218
00:16:59,442 --> 00:17:02,403
Don't distract us, Dad. We've got a king to save.

219
00:17:03,196 --> 00:17:04,489
All together, girls.

220
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:07,700
Yes! Just like in training!

221
00:17:15,583 --> 00:17:16,584
Careful!

222
00:17:34,936 --> 00:17:36,479
Bravo, my champions!

223
00:17:39,023 --> 00:17:40,858
Now that's a tackle, sisters!

224
00:17:41,192 --> 00:17:43,611
We have to do it again at the next match.

225
00:17:43,778 --> 00:17:45,738
I'm sure the fans will love it!

226
00:17:46,072 --> 00:17:47,991
"The super six-armed tackle!"

227
00:17:48,157 --> 00:17:50,493
I'll bet not even you've never seen it.

228
00:17:51,995 --> 00:17:53,746
Indeed, it's a major first.

229
00:17:57,792 --> 00:17:59,544
Thanks, girls, that was...

230
00:17:59,711 --> 00:18:01,754
Well, that was really technical!

231
00:18:02,130 --> 00:18:03,298
Bravo!

232
00:18:03,464 --> 00:18:06,509
That was perfect. Your mother would have been proud!

233
00:18:13,975 --> 00:18:16,185
Thank you for saving us, lil' pal.

234
00:18:16,352 --> 00:18:17,562
You all right, Khan?

235
00:18:18,146 --> 00:18:19,856
Winded, but I'll be fine.

236
00:18:20,023 --> 00:18:23,901
It happens a lot during matches. It'll pass in a few minutes.

237
00:18:24,902 --> 00:18:27,530
So, where are you taking us, Jojo?

238
00:18:29,115 --> 00:18:30,241
My house.

239
00:18:30,825 --> 00:18:34,037
Prince Shedar was right. I've been hiding for 16 years.

240
00:18:34,996 --> 00:18:37,749
I only leave the house to get information in Bonta

241
00:18:37,915 --> 00:18:39,667
or pay you all a visit.

242
00:18:41,627 --> 00:18:43,296
No way! Look who's here.

243
00:18:43,463 --> 00:18:46,674
Jojo and Khan Karkass, tall as ever?

244
00:18:47,383 --> 00:18:48,885
Hello, Luis.

245
00:18:49,344 --> 00:18:52,930
Hi, Luis. Between the two of us, I can't say I've missed you.

246
00:18:54,766 --> 00:18:57,185
Girls, let me introduce Luis.

247
00:18:57,352 --> 00:19:00,146
How can I describe this thing?

248
00:19:00,313 --> 00:19:03,107
He's a Shushu, an evil demon,

249
00:19:03,274 --> 00:19:05,902
but who decided to be nice from time to time.

250
00:19:06,778 --> 00:19:08,363
Lovely introduction there.

251
00:19:08,529 --> 00:19:12,325
Are you telling me that after everything we've been through,

252
00:19:12,492 --> 00:19:15,203
you never mentioned me to your daughters?

253
00:19:16,245 --> 00:19:17,497
Nope, old chum.

254
00:19:17,663 --> 00:19:20,124
I didn't want to give them nightmares.

255
00:19:22,418 --> 00:19:25,088
Open the door, Luis. The king is sick.

256
00:19:25,963 --> 00:19:29,801
Sick? More like he has one foot in the grave.

257
00:19:30,343 --> 00:19:33,805
Hey, don't say things like that! It's bad luck!

258
00:19:38,601 --> 00:19:42,105
Ladies and gentlemen, welcome to the Luis-Express!

259
00:19:44,774 --> 00:19:46,609
Don't worry, it's safe.

260
00:19:47,068 --> 00:19:49,529
If you say so, Jojo.

261
00:20:03,876 --> 00:20:05,294
Where's my wife?

262
00:20:05,586 --> 00:20:07,171
She's in the kitchen.

263
00:20:20,143 --> 00:20:21,644
Lilotte, are you there?

264
00:20:22,687 --> 00:20:24,397
Calm down! What's gotten into you?

265
00:20:24,564 --> 00:20:25,982
What's gotten into me?

266
00:20:26,149 --> 00:20:28,568
I haven't heard from you for ten days!

267
00:20:28,735 --> 00:20:30,778
So I'm not about to "calm down".

268
00:20:31,195 --> 00:20:33,865
Where did you go? I've been worried sick!

269
00:20:36,325 --> 00:20:37,160
Khan?

270
00:20:37,535 --> 00:20:40,913
Hi there, Lilotte! How have you been all this time?

271
00:20:42,540 --> 00:20:44,876
I'm so glad to see you!

272
00:20:50,131 --> 00:20:52,300
You're still sick, I see?

273
00:20:53,885 --> 00:20:56,804
Sadly, we aren't getting any younger.

274
00:20:58,055 --> 00:20:59,474
But I'm alive.

275
00:21:00,516 --> 00:21:02,685
Oh, girls, you've grown so much!

276
00:21:03,060 --> 00:21:04,687
You're so beautiful!

277
00:21:05,897 --> 00:21:07,607
Hello, Aunt Lilotte!

278
00:21:09,317 --> 00:21:12,153
I would have loved to see you more often.

279
00:21:13,112 --> 00:21:16,199
Wait... Are you injured, my dears?

280
00:21:16,908 --> 00:21:18,201
Don't worry,

281
00:21:18,367 --> 00:21:21,454
we'll be fine. There's someone worse off than us.

282
00:21:28,753 --> 00:21:29,837
His eyes...

283
00:21:31,297 --> 00:21:33,341
It's him, right? Kannell's son?

284
00:21:38,012 --> 00:21:40,473
OK, I'll take a look at his injuries.

285
00:21:40,765 --> 00:21:43,142
Then I'll take care of yours.

286
00:21:56,823 --> 00:21:58,241
I can't find any bodies.

287
00:22:05,748 --> 00:22:08,793
They survived, then. The hunt is back on, Sipho.

288
00:23:31,917 --> 00:23:35,338
Subtitling TIRAFILM

